<title>USA: Fed does not intervene in open market on Friday.</title>
<headline>Fed does not intervene in open market on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve as expected opted to stay out of the open market on Friday, analysts said.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at their 5-1/2 percent rate at the Fed's intervention time.</p>
<p>Analysts said that the coupon pass and seven-day fixed system repurchase agreements, executed on Thursday, was enough to take care of Friday's add need.</p>
<p>But they said the Fed will likely come back in the open market on Monday.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
